Note for users updating RetroArch
---------------------------------

Upstream updated the default option for 'input_driver' setting
(Settings tab --> Driver --> Input Driver) from 'udev' to 'x'. If you are
updating RetroArch from a previous installation, you may notice your keyboard to
be unresponsive. You can either include your user to the input group:

   usermod -a -G input user_name

or change 'input_driver' in ${HOME}/.config/retroarch/retroarch.cfg from

   input_driver = "udev"

to

   input_driver = "x"
